<title>USA: Greenspan shies away from commenting on stock mart.</title>
<headline>Greenspan shies away from commenting on stock mart.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan on Thursday shied away from commenting on the continued steep rise of the U.S. stock market.</p>
<p>&quot;I'll restrain myself,&quot; Greenspan told a House Banking subcommittee.</p>
<p>The Washington Post newspaper reported on Thursday that Greenspan has been worrying about the stock market's level for at least a year.</p>
